# NOTE (PLX-101): `Cargo.lock` is deliberately NOT ignored, against the usual
# convention for a library. This crate's benchmarks are decision inputs, not
# diagnostics: decision gate 2 (PLX-74/PLX-80) passed on a measured dispatch
# delta and PLX-88's attribution table produced a "leave it" verdict, both on an
# unrecorded resolution. PLX-101 measured what that costs: a routine re-resolve
# from tokio 1.48.0 to 1.53.1 moves `ladder_current/full_turn` 2.63 us -> 14.0 us
# (5.3x) with no source change. Committing the lock only pins THIS crate's own
# builds, tests and benches — a `tokio = "1.0"` caret dependency still resolves
# freely for anyone who depends on plexus-core. See benches/common/resolution.rs.

